# DECISIONS.md — decisions taken during implementation

Design decisions live in the design doc (`Docs/DESIGN_v0.md`, "Decisions needed"). This file records the smaller calls made while building, so nobody re-litigates them by accident, and the questions that are waiting for Bryan. The orchestrator appends; Bryan edits.

## Taken (October 14, 2026, kickoff)

| # | Decision | Why | Where it lives |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| K1 | The PC hosts the simulation; the Quest is a client; browser pages are the Plan seat and the 2D Site fallback for good | One protocol, one truth; Zoom and no-headset play for free; the Unity host can be skipped for the demo | `Docs/PROTOCOL.md`, `Docs/ROADMAP.md` |
| K2 | Phase 0 is HTML and Node first, Unity after the table test | The three seats and the kit can be table-tested in days; the C# port then has an oracle | `Docs/ORCHESTRATOR.md` |
| K3 | `rateDrop` is the fraction lost; a crew works at `1 - rateDrop` | Matches the workbook's "Base Rate Drop" column | `Data/catalog.json`, `Docs/SCENARIO_SCHEMA.md` |
| K4 | Authored events always fire; protection changes severity, not likelihood | Stage 2's identical seed must meet the same collapse; the catalog's likelihood multipliers are kept for a later random mode | scenario `rules.likelihoodRollsApply` |
| K5 | A trench box is bought for a stretch (from–to) and is in place while the pipe crew works inside it; a stretch that misses the collapse station is deviation F3 | Gives Plan a station to name and Site a thing to check | `protect` op |
| K6 | Durations under protection round to the nearest half day | Keeps the arithmetic on the front page readable | WO-02 |
| K7 | A conflict argument fires once per crew pair per stage; afterwards a trailing crew that catches its leader idles against it, bills and gets angrier, with no second argument | The foremen have had it out once; a re-firing argument would deadlock any plan with one hold | WO-02 |
| K8 | After a stop-work, any Plan commit lifts it for the zone's crews unless the commit holds them | The doc's "stands until Plan commits a plan or resumes" | WO-02 |
| K9 | Overhead (30%) applies to crew billing and protection daily fees; purchases, mobilization, fees and fines at face value | Simplest reading of "30% of direct spend"; the result card shows both | WO-02 |
| K10 | Codes are `dddd-c` with `c = digit sum mod 10`; Rules checks the digits before reading a code | Paper edgework the Rules seat can do without the build | `kit.checkDigit` |
| K11 | F1 applies to the first hold or lend delivered by radio, whichever crew it hits | Rewards Site's positioning instead of scripting one crew | scenario `deviations` |
| K12 | The drainage pump restores excavation and backfill to 100% during rain (workbook A2-D) and halves the new rework rule | Keeps the workbook's effect and adds the pull lesson | scenario A2 options |
| K13 | Stage 2 keeps Stage 1's contract (promise Day 35, budget $278,400, deadline Day 47) | The overlay compares like with like | `stage2_texas.json` |
| K14 | Stage 2's example plan moves backfill to Day 12 (not 11) | Day 12 is the zero-idle start with no events; with the collapse it still holds | design doc, `stage2_texas.json` note |
| K15 | An in-house lend moves the machine along the haul road the same day (`|Δft| / 1500` hours); the city's remobilization delay applies to `remob` after a demobilization and to hired machines' lead time | A machine 400 ft up the trench does not take a day to arrive; the order lag (next shift unless Site is there) already costs the day the design wants | WO-02, manual P1-A, P-4 |
| K16 | Rain rework is evaluated at the rain's end over the feet open at its start; a pump paid for before the rain ends halves it; the pump also restores excavation and backfill to full rate during the rain (workbook A2-D) | Lets the forecast matter: `pay` is allowed from the forecast day | WO-02 |

## Open (for Bryan; the orchestrator adds a line when a work order surfaces one)

| # | Question | Recommended answer | Needed by |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| O1 | Working title | LOB, Over (a radio sign-off; talk is the mechanic). Alternatives: LOB Radio; Three LOB | Kit cover (WO-04); can be changed in one place later |
| O2 | City fine for pushing past a permit boundary | $10,000 placeholder in the scenarios, marked `_validate` | Table test |
| O3 | Open-trench limit for the Texas city | 2 zones (3,000 ft) as the permit count; validators may prefer a footage rule | Table test |
| O4 | Demobilization fee and delay | $5,000 and the city's 1–3 days | Table test |
| O5 | Rain rework rule | 1 day per 500 ft open, pump halves | Table test |
| O6 | Drainage pump price | $4,000 + $60 a day placeholder | Table test |
| O7 | Which of F1–F5 are frequent enough on real jobs to teach | Keep F1, F2, F3 for the Texas stages; F4 and F5 for Stage 3 | Stage 3 authoring |
| O8 | P1 option A's "Day 2/1/0" column in the workbook versus the game's 3/2/1 clearing days | Keep 3/2/1 for both own and hired machines until Phumpat says otherwise | Table test |
| O9 | Stage 1 finish under the full rules (order lag, 2-day clearing, rain at 50% plus 1 day of rework per 500 ft open) lands later than the design doc's "36 to 38", likely 38 to 41 against the promise of 35 and the deadline of 47 | Let WO-02's scripted run report the number, then either keep it (push hurts more) or soften the rework rule to half a day per 500 ft; update the design doc's Stage 1 table from the measured run | After WO-02 |
| O10 | F2 (pushing ahead) at the job start: the simulation treats 0 ft as an unpermitted boundary when zone 1's code is not entered, so in Stage 2 the excavator overshoots, the $10,000 fine lands on the first tick, and the once-per-stage F2 is spent before the real zone 3 boundary (review of WO-02, `permits.js` / `deviations.js`). WO-02's wording ("the first time exc reaches an unpermitted boundary") supports the code; the design's ("crosses one") suggests a boundary between zones | Exclude the job start from F2: at 0 ft an unpermitted excavator idles and bills, no overshoot, no fine. Until then the facilitator keeps the host paused through the huddle and Plan enters zone 1's code before Start (the host starts paused, WO-03) | Before the Stage 2 table test |
| O11 | Stop-work lift has no radio lag: any Plan commit lifts a stop-work for every crew at the commit instant (K8 is silent on lag), while a `resume` op lands by the next-shift rule. In the Stage 1 script the excavator digs from t 5.1 to 6.04 after the stop because the lift was instant while the lend was F1-ignored | Apply the order-lag rule to the lift (lands next shift unless Site is at the station), so the stop-work behaves like every other order | Phase 0.5 sim pass, with O10 |
| O12 | Conflict detection uses the leader's `rate x mult`, so a leader idling at a permit boundary or hold point (mult 1, moving 0 ft) never triggers an argument and the trailer silently idles against it; pipe can therefore never argue with excavation in these stages (crane 180 < excavator 220). Matches WO-02's formula; flagged against the design's "would cross its leader within the next day" | Keep as is for the table test (an argument fires only when both would move); revisit if the Stage 2 test wants an argument at a hold point | Stage 3 authoring |

## How to add a line

Taken: number, one-line decision, one-line reason, where it lives. Open: the question, your recommended answer, when it is needed. Never delete a Taken line; strike it and add the replacement.
### 2. The crew model (must match the oracle exactly in `pure` mode)

- `t` in days, `t = 0` is the morning of Day 1; a crew with `startDay` N starts at `t = N - 1`.
- Each tick, in order `exc`, `pipe`, `back`: if started and not finished, `limit = min(lengthFt, leaderPos)` where exc has no leader, pipe's leader is exc, back's leader is pipe; `newPos = min(pos + rate * mult * dt, limit)`; `work += (newPos - pos) / rate` when it moved; `pos = newPos`; finished when `pos >= lengthFt - 1e-6`.
- `rate` = the crew's current machine's `rateFtPerDay`; `mult` = product of active modifiers (event rate drops as `1 - rateDrop`, rain 0.5, hold/stop/arguing/demobilized/lent-away 0, rework 0 for pipe).
- Peak open trench = max over ticks of `exc.pos - back.pos`.
- Idle days per crew = (finish - start) - work. Crew cost = Σ daily machine cost × days on site × (1 + overheadRate). Days on site end at the crew's own finish, or at demobilization.
- Optional WIP cap (`pure` mode only, for the golden `pull_distance_*` case): exc `limit = min(limit, back.pos + capFt)`.
- `pure` mode disables events, deviations, permits, hold points, orders landing late and conflicts; it exists only to prove the crew model. Everything else uses the full model.

### 3. The full model (rules; every constant comes from the scenario or the catalog, never from code)

- **Speed.** `full` normally; `slow` from the moment an event fires until the next Plan `commit`; `paused` by facilitator `ctrl`. Speed is the host's pacing concern; the sim only exposes it.
- **Orders.** A `commit` turns each op into an `Order {id, op, crew, issuedT, landsT, status}`. `landsT = issuedT` if the Site truck is dismounted within 100 ft of that crew's current position, else the next shift boundary `Math.floor(issuedT) + 1`. Orders apply when they land. `setStart`, `enterPermit`, `enterInspection` and `pay` apply at once (office actions). `radio` re-issues an order with a fresh `landsT` by the same rule. A commit is all-or-none: validate every op first (nack reasons below), then apply.
- **setStart.** `setStart {crew, day}`: nack `"plan locked"` when `plan.locked` or the crew's `locked` is true, nack `"crew already started"` when `t >= crew.startDay - 1`; otherwise the crew's `startDay` becomes `day` (whole days, `>= displayDay`).
- **Hold / resume.** `hold {crew, fromDay?, days?}`: from landing (or from `fromDay` if later) the crew's `mult` is 0 and it bills; with `days` the hold ends by itself after `days`, without it the hold stands until `resume`. `resume` lifts a hold or a stop-work for that crew. Any Plan `commit` after a stop-work lifts the stop-work for the zone's crews unless the commit holds them (design: "stands until Plan commits a plan or resumes").
- **Lend.** `lend {machine, toCrew, days}`: the lender's `mult` is 0 from landing; the machine moves along the haul road and arrives at `toCrew` after `|Δft| / 1500 / 24` days (same day; the city's remobilization delay applies only to `remob` and to hired machines, decision K15). A `lend` of the excavation crew's machine to `pipe` while a P1 is active is the `clear_own` response: the arrival starts the clearing, the lender stays at 0 for the clearing days (`lenderLosesSameDays`), then the machine returns the same way. Otherwise the machine works for `toCrew` for `days` (the receiving crew's rate becomes the lent machine's rate while it has no machine of its own; a crew with its own machine plus a lent one adds the lent rate) and returns.
- **Order a machine.** `order {machine}`: price + `mobilizationUsd` charged at commit; arrives after `leadDays.normal + cities[city].leadDelayDays`; on arrival it replaces the crew's machine (the old one is released at half its price). `pay {item: "hire_excavator", machine}` during an active P1 is the hired-clearing response: same charges and lead time, it clears the collapse in the clearing days for its `sizeClass`, then is released at half price. Rush orders are not exposed (catalog `rushExposedToPlayers: false`).
- **Protect.** `protect {kind, fromFt, toFt}`: price at commit, daily cost while any crew works inside the stretch; `trench_slope` refused in `slopeRefused` cities; `preparationAllowed: false` → nack `"not in the budget"` plus the `prepRefused` voice trigger for `protect` and `order` at any time in that stage (the PM refuses purchases ahead; `pay` for an active or forecast event's options is always allowed).
"""Typeset the authored field manual and scenario cards: python Paper/make_kit.py SCENARIO."""

import argparse
import json
import re
from pathlib import Path
from xml.sax.saxutils import escape

import reportlab
from reportlab.lib import colors
from reportlab.lib.pagesizes import landscape, letter
from reportlab.lib.styles import ParagraphStyle
from reportlab.lib.units import inch
from reportlab.pdfgen import canvas
from reportlab.pdfbase import pdfmetrics
from reportlab.pdfbase.ttfonts import TTFont
from reportlab.platypus import Paragraph, Table, TableStyle


PAPER = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
ROOT = PAPER.parent
MARGIN = 42
WIDTH, HEIGHT = letter
TEXT_WIDTH = WIDTH - 2 * MARGIN
STATION_LABEL_FT = 500  # WO-04: ledger labels every 500 ft.
TOKEN_DIAMETER = 2 * inch  # WO-04: two-inch circles, printed at actual size.
CARDS_PER_PAGE = 4  # WO-04: four permit/inspection cards per sheet.
TOKENS_PER_PAGE = 12  # Letter layout: three columns of four two-inch circles.
SEATS = "Site / Plan / Rules"  # WO-04: the three seats on the cover.
RETURN_INSTRUCTION = (
    "Read the code to Plan. Return this card when the zone is backfilled and signed."
)
SECTION = re.compile(r"^## (.+?) \(([^)]+)\)\s*$", re.MULTILINE)
PLACEHOLDER = re.compile(r"\{\{([^{}]+)\}\}")


def register_fonts():
    # ReportLab ships these fonts; embedding keeps the manual's math glyphs printable.
    font_dir = Path(reportlab.__file__).parent / "fonts"
    for name, filename in (
        ("KitSans", "Vera.ttf"), ("KitSans-Bold", "VeraBd.ttf"),
        ("KitSans-Italic", "VeraIt.ttf"), ("KitSans-BoldItalic", "VeraBI.ttf"),
    ):
        pdfmetrics.registerFont(TTFont(name, str(font_dir / filename)))
    pdfmetrics.registerFontFamily(
        "KitSans", normal="KitSans", bold="KitSans-Bold",
        italic="KitSans-Italic", boldItalic="KitSans-BoldItalic",
    )


def read_json(path):
    return json.loads(Path(path).read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig"))


def markdown_table(headers, rows):
    return "\n".join(
        "| " + " | ".join(map(str, row)) + " |"
        for row in [headers, ["---"] * len(headers), *rows]
    )


def fill_placeholders(text, scenario, catalog, missing):
    zones = scenario["job"]["zones"]
    permits = scenario["permits"]
    inspections = scenario["inspections"]
    derived = {
        "job.zoneCount": len(zones),
        "job.zoneLengthFt": zones[0]["toFt"] - zones[0]["fromFt"],
        "permits.heldByText": (
            "all issued and posted by the PM before Day 1"
            if permits["heldBy"] == "pm"
            else f"held by Rules; the city allows {permits['openZoneLimit']} zone(s) open at a time"
        ),
        "permits.cardsTable": markdown_table(
            ["Zone", "Permit number", "Code"],
            [[c["zone"], c["number"], c["code"]] for c in permits["cards"]],
        ),
        "inspections.cardsTable": markdown_table(
            ["Zone", "Inspection card number"],
            [[c["zone"], c["number"]] for c in inspections["cards"]],
        ),
        "inspections.checklistBullets": "\n".join(
            f"- [ ] {item}" for item in inspections["checklist"]
        ),
    }

    def replace(match):
        key = match[1].strip()
        if key in derived:
            return str(derived[key])
        parts = key.split(".")
        # Never expose event/deviation payloads or author-only metadata via a template.
        forbidden = {"events", "deviations", "effect", "trigger", "cardWhenProtected"}
        if not any(p.startswith("_") or p in forbidden for p in parts):
            source = {**catalog, **scenario, "city": catalog["cities"][scenario["city"]]}
            try:
                for part in parts:
                    source = source[part]
                if isinstance(source, (str, int, float, bool)):
                    return str(source)
            except (KeyError, TypeError):
                pass
        missing.add(key)
        return "[to validate]"

    return PLACEHOLDER.sub(replace, text)


def manual_sections(source, scenario, catalog):
    headings = list(SECTION.finditer(source))
    sections = {}
    for index, heading in enumerate(headings):
        end = headings[index + 1].start() if index + 1 < len(headings) else len(source)
        body = source[heading.end():end].strip()
        for section_id in heading[2].split(","):
            sections[section_id.strip()] = (heading[1], body)
    missing = set()
    selected = []
    for section_id in scenario["kit"]["manualPages"]:
        if section_id not in sections:
            raise ValueError(f"manual_v0.md has no section {section_id!r}")
        title, body = sections[section_id]
        selected.append((section_id, title, fill_placeholders(body, scenario, catalog, missing)))
    # The typesetting note is author instruction, not player-facing manual text.
    preface = source[:headings[0].start()].split("Typesetting notes", 1)[0].strip()
    return preface, selected, missing


def inline(text):
    text = escape(text)
    text = re.sub(r"\*\*(.+?)\*\*", r"<b>\1</b>", text)
    return re.sub(r"\*([^*]+)\*", r"<i>\1</i>", text)


def plain(text):
    result = []
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if line.strip() == "---" or re.fullmatch(r"[| :\-]+", line.strip()):
            continue
        line = re.sub(r"^#{1,6} ", "", line)
        line = line.replace("**", "").replace("*", "")
        if line.startswith("|"):
            line = " | ".join(cell.strip() for cell in line.strip("|").split("|"))
        result.append(line)
    return "\n".join(result).strip()


def paragraph(text, size=10.5, bold=False, **kwargs):
    style = ParagraphStyle(
        "kit", fontName="KitSans-Bold" if bold else "KitSans",
        fontSize=size, leading=size * 1.24, spaceAfter=6, **kwargs,
    )
    return Paragraph(inline(text), style)


def table_widths(headers, width):
    count = len(headers)
    if count == 2:
        fractions = [0.24, 0.76]
    elif headers[0] == "Option":
        fractions = [0.23, 0.45, 0.32]
    elif headers[0] == "Site says":
        fractions = [0.35, 0.18, 0.32, 0.15]
    elif headers[0] == "Hazard":
        fractions = [0.22, 0.12, 0.66]
    elif headers[0] == "Kind":
        fractions = [0.23, 0.12, 0.12, 0.23, 0.30]
    elif headers[0] == "Machine":
        fractions = [0.32, 0.14, 0.16, 0.18, 0.20]
    else:
        fractions = [1 / count] * count
    return [fraction * width for fraction in fractions]


def flowables(markdown, width, size=10.5):
    lines = markdown.splitlines()
    blocks = []
    i = 0
    while i < len(lines):
        line = lines[i].strip()
        i += 1
        if not line or line == "---":
            continue
        if line.startswith("|"):
            rows = [line]
            while i < len(lines) and lines[i].strip().startswith("|"):
                rows.append(lines[i].strip())
                i += 1
            cells = [[cell.strip() for cell in row.strip("|").split("|")] for row in rows]
            cells = [row for row in cells if not all(re.fullmatch(r":?-+:?", c) for c in row)]
            has_header = any(cells[0])
            if not has_header:
                cells.pop(0)
            widths = table_widths(cells[0] if has_header else ["", ""], width)
            data = [[paragraph(c, size - 0.3, bold=has_header and r == 0)
                     for c in row] for r, row in enumerate(cells)]
            table = Table(data, colWidths=widths, hAlign="LEFT")
            styles = [
                ("GRID", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 0.5, colors.black),
                ("VALIGN", (0, 0), (-1, -1), "TOP"),
                ("LEFTPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 6),
                ("RIGHTPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 6),
                ("TOPPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 4),
                ("BOTTOMPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 4),
            ]
            if has_header:
                styles.append(("BACKGROUND", (0, 0), (-1, 0), colors.Color(0.94, 0.94, 0.94)))
            table.setStyle(TableStyle(styles))
            table.spaceAfter = 10
            blocks.append(table)
        elif match := re.match(r"^#{1,3} (.+)", line):
            blocks.append(paragraph(match[1], size + 2, bold=True))
        elif match := re.match(r"(\d+)\. (Site|Plan|Rules): (.*)", line):
            # Put the named seat in a separate margin without changing the procedure.
            table = Table([[
                paragraph(match[1] + ".", size), paragraph(match[2] + ":", size, bold=True),
                paragraph(match[3], size),
            ]], colWidths=[22, 46, width - 68])
            table.setStyle(TableStyle([
                ("VALIGN", (0, 0), (-1, -1), "TOP"),
                ("LEFTPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 0),
                ("RIGHTPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 3),
                ("TOPPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 0),
                ("BOTTOMPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 4),
            ]))
            blocks.append(table)
        elif line.startswith("- "):
            blocks.append(paragraph(line[2:], size, leftIndent=12, bulletIndent=0, bulletText="\u2022"))
        else:
            while (i < len(lines) and lines[i].strip()
                   and not re.match(r"^(?:\||#|- |\d+\.)", lines[i].strip())):
                line += " " + lines[i].strip()
                i += 1
            blocks.append(paragraph(line, size))
    return blocks


def block_height(block, width):
    return block.wrap(width, HEIGHT)[1] + block.getSpaceAfter()


def draw_blocks(pdf, blocks, x, top, width):
    for block in blocks:
        _, height = block.wrap(width, HEIGHT)
        block.drawOn(pdf, x, top - height)
        top -= height + block.getSpaceAfter()
    return top


def new_pdf(path, page_size=letter):
    # Invariant metadata makes reruns reproducible for the same authored inputs.
    pdf = canvas.Canvas(str(path), pagesize=page_size, invariant=1, pageCompression=1)
    pdf.setTitle(path.stem)
    pdf.setAuthor("LOB, Over")
    return pdf


def footer(pdf, stage_id, page, page_size=letter):
    width, _ = page_size
    pdf.setLineWidth(0.6)
    pdf.line(MARGIN, 34, width - MARGIN, 34)
    pdf.setFont("KitSans", 8)
    pdf.drawString(MARGIN, 21, stage_id)
    pdf.drawRightString(width - MARGIN, 21, str(page))


def section_page(pdf, stage_id, page, title, markdown):
    heading = paragraph(title, 18, bold=True)
    heading_height = heading.wrap(TEXT_WIDTH, HEIGHT)[1]
    top = HEIGHT - MARGIN
    heading.drawOn(pdf, MARGIN, top - heading_height)
    content_top = top - heading_height - 19
    pdf.setLineWidth(1.2)
    pdf.line(MARGIN, content_top + 9, WIDTH - MARGIN, content_top + 9)
    available = content_top - 48
    for size in [10.5, 10, 9.5, 9, 8.5]:
        blocks = flowables(markdown, TEXT_WIDTH, size)
        if sum(block_height(b, TEXT_WIDTH) for b in blocks) <= available:
            draw_blocks(pdf, blocks, MARGIN, content_top, TEXT_WIDTH)
            footer(pdf, stage_id, page)
            pdf.showPage()
            return
    raise ValueError(f"Manual section does not fit one readable page: {title}")


def make_manual(out, scenario, catalog, source):
    preface, sections, missing = manual_sections(source, scenario, catalog)
    pdf = new_pdf(out / "manual.pdf")
    draw_blocks(pdf, [paragraph(scenario["title"], 30, bold=True)], MARGIN, 661, TEXT_WIDTH)
    draw_blocks(pdf, flowables(preface, TEXT_WIDTH, 12), MARGIN, 570, TEXT_WIDTH)
    pdf.setLineWidth(2)
    pdf.line(MARGIN, 340, WIDTH - MARGIN, 340)
    pdf.setFont("KitSans-Bold", 20)
    pdf.drawString(MARGIN, 301, SEATS)
    pdf.setFont("KitSans-Bold", 15)
    pdf.drawString(MARGIN, 265, "Rules seat only")
    footer(pdf, scenario["id"], 1)
    pdf.showPage()
    plain_parts = [scenario["title"], plain(preface), SEATS, "Rules seat only"]
    page = 2
    for section_id, title, markdown in sections:
        plain_parts.extend([title, plain(markdown)])
        if section_id == "procedures":
            # Keep each procedure together; six procedures occupy two legible pages.
            split = markdown.index("**P-4 ")
            pieces = [markdown[:split], markdown[split:]]
        else:
            pieces = [markdown]
        for index, piece in enumerate(pieces):
            heading = title if index == 0 else title + " (continued)"
            section_page(pdf, scenario["id"], page, heading, piece)
            page += 1
    pdf.save()
    (out / "manual.txt").write_text("\n\n".join(plain_parts) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    return missing


def cut_rectangle(pdf, x, y, width, height):
    pdf.saveState()
    pdf.setDash(3, 3)
    pdf.setLineWidth(0.5)
    pdf.rect(x, y, width, height)
    pdf.restoreState()


def draw_text(pdf, text, x, top, width, size=11, bold=False):
    block = paragraph(text, size, bold=bold)
    _, height = block.wrap(width, HEIGHT)
    block.drawOn(pdf, x, top - height)
    return top - height


def make_cards(out, scenario):
    pdf = new_pdf(out / "cards.pdf")
    cards = [(kind, card) for kind in ("permits", "inspections") for card in scenario[kind]["cards"]]
    card_width, card_height = 252, 324
    for i, (kind, card) in enumerate(cards):
        slot = i % CARDS_PER_PAGE
        x = MARGIN + (slot % 2) * 276
        y = 408 if slot < 2 else 66
        cut_rectangle(pdf, x, y, card_width, card_height)
        left, top, inside = x + 16, y + card_height - 18, card_width - 32
        if kind == "permits":
            label = "ISSUED BY PM" if scenario["permits"]["heldBy"] == "pm" else "PERMIT"
        else:
            label = "INSPECTION"
        draw_text(pdf, label, left, top, inside, 12, True)
        draw_text(pdf, f"Zone {card['zone']}", left, top - 35, inside, 24, True)
        if kind == "permits":
            draw_text(pdf, card["number"], left, top - 82, inside, 18)
            draw_text(pdf, card["code"], left, top - 121, inside, 34, True)
            draw_text(pdf, RETURN_INSTRUCTION, left, top - 190, inside, 11)
        else:
            draw_text(pdf, card["number"], left, top - 77, inside, 26, True)
            checklist_top = top - 124
            for item in scenario["inspections"]["checklist"]:
                pdf.rect(left, checklist_top - 9, 9, 9)
                bottom = draw_text(pdf, item, left + 17, checklist_top + 1, inside - 17, 10)
                checklist_top = bottom - 14
            pdf.line(left, y + 40, x + card_width - 16, y + 40)
            draw_text(pdf, "Rules signature", left, y + 34, inside, 8)
        if slot == CARDS_PER_PAGE - 1 or i == len(cards) - 1:
            footer(pdf, scenario["id"], i // CARDS_PER_PAGE + 1)
            pdf.showPage()
    pdf.save()


def station(feet):
    feet = int(feet)
    return f"{feet // 100}+{feet % 100:02d}"


def make_ledger(out, scenario):
    size = landscape(letter)
    pdf = new_pdf(out / "ledger.pdf", size)
    left, right, top = 139, 750, 472
    length = scenario["job"]["lengthFt"]

    def position(feet):
        return left + (right - left) * feet / length

    for copy in (1, 2):  # WO-04: two copies of the ledger.
        draw_text(pdf, scenario["title"] + " — Zone ledger", MARGIN, 570, 708, 19, True)
        for zone in scenario["job"]["zones"]:
            center = position((zone["fromFt"] + zone["toFt"]) / 2)
            pdf.setFont("KitSans-Bold", 10)
            pdf.drawCentredString(center, 516, f"Zone {zone['id']}")
        pdf.setFont("KitSans", 8)
        for feet in range(0, length + 1, STATION_LABEL_FT):
            x = position(feet)
            pdf.drawCentredString(x, 492, station(feet))
            pdf.setLineWidth(0.35)
            pdf.line(x, top, x, top - 186)
        for row, crew in enumerate(scenario["crews"]):
            draw_text(pdf, crew["name"], MARGIN, top - row * 62 - 22, left - MARGIN - 8, 10, True)
        for row in range(4):
            pdf.line(left, top - row * 62, right, top - row * 62)
        box_top, box_bottom = 246, 102
        labels = ["Permit day", "Pipe complete day", "Inspection day", "Backfill day"]
        for row, label in enumerate(labels):
            draw_text(pdf, label, MARGIN, box_top - row * 36 - 11, left - MARGIN - 8, 9)
        for row in range(5):
            pdf.setLineWidth(0.5)
            pdf.line(left, box_top - row * 36, right, box_top - row * 36)
        boundaries = sorted({ft for z in scenario["job"]["zones"] for ft in (z["fromFt"], z["toFt"])})
        for feet in boundaries:
            pdf.setLineWidth(1.6)
            x = position(feet)
            pdf.line(x, top, x, top - 186)
            pdf.line(x, box_top, x, box_bottom)
        footer(pdf, scenario["id"], copy, size)
        pdf.showPage()
    pdf.save()


def make_tokens(out, scenario):
    token_ft = scenario["kit"]["openTrenchTokenFt"]
    count, remainder = divmod(scenario["job"]["lengthFt"], token_ft)
    if remainder:
        raise ValueError("Job length must be a whole number of open-trench tokens")
    pdf = new_pdf(out / "tokens.pdf")
    for i in range(count):
        slot = i % TOKENS_PER_PAGE
        x = 138 + (slot % 3) * 168
        y = 648 - (slot // 3) * 168
        pdf.saveState()
        pdf.setDash(3, 3)
        pdf.setLineWidth(0.7)
        pdf.circle(x, y, TOKEN_DIAMETER / 2)
        pdf.restoreState()
        pdf.setFont("KitSans-Bold", 16)
        pdf.drawCentredString(x, y - 5, f"{token_ft} ft open")
        if slot == TOKENS_PER_PAGE - 1 or i == count - 1:
            footer(pdf, scenario["id"], i // TOKENS_PER_PAGE + 1)
            pdf.showPage()
    pdf.save()


def make_jobsign(out, scenario):
    pdf = new_pdf(out / "jobsign.pdf")
    sign = scenario["job"]["sign"]
    cut_rectangle(pdf, 60, 276, 492, 300)
    draw_text(pdf, scenario["title"], 84, 550, 444, 24, True)
    draw_text(pdf, sign["cityCode"], 84, 495, 444, 48, True)
    draw_text(pdf, sign["pipe"], 84, 415, 444, 21)
    draw_text(pdf, f"{sign['contractDays']} contract days", 84, 345, 444, 25, True)
    footer(pdf, scenario["id"], 1)
    pdf.showPage()
    pdf.save()


def make_index(out, scenario):
    lines = [f"permit zone {c['zone']} {c['number']} {c['code']}" for c in scenario["permits"]["cards"]]
    lines.extend(f"inspection zone {c['zone']} {c['number']}" for c in scenario["inspections"]["cards"])
    (out / "kit_index.txt").write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")


def make_kit(scenario_path, out=None):
    register_fonts()
    scenario = read_json(scenario_path)
    catalog = read_json(ROOT / "Data" / "catalog.json")
    source = (PAPER / "manual_v0.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig")
    out = Path(out) if out else PAPER / "out" / scenario["id"]
    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    missing = make_manual(out, scenario, catalog, source)
    make_cards(out, scenario)
    make_ledger(out, scenario)
    make_tokens(out, scenario)
    make_jobsign(out, scenario)
    make_index(out, scenario)
    print(f"{scenario['id']}: wrote 5 PDFs, manual.txt and kit_index.txt to {out}")
    print("Unresolved placeholders: " + (", ".join(sorted(missing)) if missing else "none"))
    return out


def main():
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
    parser.add_argument("scenario", type=Path)
    parser.add_argument("--out", type=Path, help="Output directory (default: Paper/out/<scenario id>)")
    args = parser.parse_args()
    make_kit(args.scenario, args.out)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
import { CREW_IDS, EPS, HOURS_PER_DAY, activeCollapse, crewAt, emit, nearby, travelDays, voice, zoneAt } from './common.js';
import { confirmDeviation, inspectProtection } from './deviations.js';
import { inspectionText, stakeAt } from './views.js';

const TARGETS = new Set(['wall', 'water', 'pipe', 'machine', 'protection', 'board', 'sky', 'ticket', 'crew']);
export function applySite(s, cmd) {
  const truck = s.truck;
  if (cmd.action === 'moveTo') {
    if (truck.moving || truck.dismounted) return 'mount before moving';
    if (!Number.isFinite(cmd.stationFt) || cmd.stationFt < 0 || cmd.stationFt > s.scenario.job.lengthFt) return 'invalid station';
    truck.fromFt = truck.stationFt;
    truck.toFt = cmd.stationFt;
    truck.departT = s.t;
    truck.arrivesT = s.t + travelDays(truck.stationFt, cmd.stationFt);
    truck.moving = truck.arrivesT > s.t;
    return;
  }
  if (cmd.action === 'mount' || cmd.action === 'dismount') {
    if (truck.moving) return 'truck moving';
    truck.dismounted = cmd.action === 'dismount';
    return;
  }
  if (!truck.dismounted || truck.moving) return 'dismount first';
  if (cmd.action === 'inspect') {
    if (!TARGETS.has(cmd.target)) return 'unknown inspection target';
    const ft = stakeAt(s, truck.stationFt);
    if (cmd.target === 'protection') inspectProtection(s, ft);
    const event = activeCollapse(s);
    if (event && stakeAt(s, event.stationFt) === ft) event.inspected = true;
    emit(s, 'inspection', { id: cmd.id, target: cmd.target, text: inspectionText(s, cmd.target), seats: ['site'] });
    return;
  }
  if (cmd.action === 'flag') {
    // Protocol caps authored notes at 40 characters.
    const MAX_NOTE_LENGTH = 40;
    if (!Number.isFinite(cmd.stationFt) || cmd.stationFt < 0 || cmd.stationFt > s.scenario.job.lengthFt
      || cmd.note != null && (typeof cmd.note !== 'string' || cmd.note.length > MAX_NOTE_LENGTH)) return 'invalid flag';
    s.flags.push({ stationFt: cmd.stationFt, day: s.t, ...(cmd.note ? { note: cmd.note } : {}) });
    return;
  }
  if (cmd.action === 'stopWork') {
    if (zoneAt(s, truck.stationFt)?.id !== cmd.zone) return 'outside zone';
    for (const id of CREW_IDS) {
      const c = s.crews[id];
      if (zoneAt(s, c.pos)?.id === cmd.zone) c.stop = { zone: cmd.zone,
        fromT: s.t + s.scenario.rules.stopWorkReachHours / HOURS_PER_DAY };
    }
    return;
  }
  if (cmd.action === 'confirm') {
    const order = s.orders.find(order => order.id === cmd.orderId);
    if (!order?.crew || order.landedT == null || order.status === 'sent'
      || !nearby(s, s.crews[order.crew].pos)) return 'order not landed here';
    if (!['done', 'notDone'].includes(cmd.outcome)) return 'invalid outcome';
    order.status = cmd.outcome === 'done' ? 'confirmed' : 'notCarriedOut';
    confirmDeviation(s, order, cmd.outcome);
    if (cmd.outcome === 'notDone') voice(s, 'orderNotDone', ['plan']);
    return;
  }
  if (cmd.action === 'listen') {
    const c = crewAt(s);
    if (c?.arguing) {
      const conflict = s.conflicts.find(conflict => conflict.trailing === c.id || conflict.leader === c.id);
      voice(s, 'conflict', ['site'], [conflict.trailing, conflict.leader]);
    } else if (c && (c.status === 'held' || c.status === 'stopped') && c.mood > 0) {
      voice(s, `heldDay${c.mood}`, ['site'], [c.id]);
    } else emit(s, 'inspection', { id: cmd.id, target: 'crew', text: 'Nothing to hear.', seats: ['site'] });
    return;
  }
  return 'unknown action';
}

export function updateTruck(s) {
  const truck = s.truck;
  if (!truck.moving) return;
  if (s.t >= truck.arrivesT - EPS) {
    truck.stationFt = truck.toFt;
    truck.moving = false;
  } else truck.stationFt = truck.fromFt + (truck.toFt - truck.fromFt)
    * (s.t - truck.departT) / (truck.arrivesT - truck.departT);
}
import { LEADER, EPS, CONFLICT_LOOKAHEAD_DAYS, emit, voice } from './common.js';

export function detectConflicts(s) {
  for (const [trailingId, leaderId] of Object.entries(LEADER)) {
    const trailing = s.crews[trailingId], leader = s.crews[leaderId];
    const key = `${trailingId}:${leaderId}`;
    // A completed leader has left the workfront; the job endpoint cannot be crossed.
    if (leader.finishT != null || s.conflicts.some(c => c.pair === key)
      || trailing.mult <= 0 || trailing.pos >= leader.pos - EPS) continue;
    if (trailing.pos + trailing.rate * trailing.mult * CONFLICT_LOOKAHEAD_DAYS
      <= leader.pos + leader.rate * leader.mult * CONFLICT_LOOKAHEAD_DAYS + EPS) continue;
    s.conflicts.push({ pair: key, trailing: trailingId, leader: leaderId, firedT: s.t, resolved: false });
    trailing.arguing = leader.arguing = true;
    trailing.mult = leader.mult = 0;
    trailing.status = leader.status = 'arguing';
    s.speed = 'slow';
    voice(s, 'conflict', ['site'], [trailingId, leaderId]);
    emit(s, 'event', { eventId: `conflict_${trailingId}_${leaderId}`, day: s.t,
      stationFt: trailing.pos, zone: null, seats: ['site'],
      card: { title: 'Crews stopped', facts: [`${trailing.name} and ${leader.name} foremen are arguing.`] } });
  }
}

export function validateConflictCommit(s, ops) {
  if (s.conflicts.some(c => !c.resolved && !ops.some(op => op?.crew === c.trailing
    && (op.op === 'hold' || op.op === 'demob')))) return 'conflict: hold or demobilize the trailing crew';
}

export function resolveConflicts(s) {
  for (const conflict of s.conflicts.filter(c => !c.resolved)) {
    conflict.resolved = true;
    conflict.resolvedT = s.t;
    // The trailing crew waits for its field order; only the leader resumes at commit.
    s.crews[conflict.leader].arguing = false;
  }
}

