Paper\manual_v0.md:132:| B. Hire more equipment | Rate back up after arrival; price + $25,000 mobilization; lead days 
from the catalog + this city's delay | Lead days (Rules, city page); budget (Plan) |
Paper\manual_v0.md:173:| B. Emergency shoring | Work resumes in 1 day. $18,000 plus $150 a day for the rest of the job 
| Budget (Plan) |
Paper\manual_v0.md:174:| C. Hire an outside excavator | Clears in 3/2/1 days by size after the catalog lead days + 
this city's delay; price + $25,000 mobilization | Lead days (Rules); budget (Plan) |
Paper\manual_v0.md:176:**Before it happens.** Where Site reports seepage and a soft toe (indicator table, first row), 
protection bought ahead changes the collapse, not the chance of it in this game: a trench box ($14,000 + $90 a day) 
halves the clearing time; shoring ($32,000 + $180 a day) cuts it to 0.4; sloping ($6,000) to 0.7 and is refused in New 
York, Los Angeles and Bangkok. The box must cover the stretch Site named; Site confirms where it stands.
Paper\manual_v0.md:280:| D. Rent a drainage pump now | Excavation and backfill back to 100% during the rain; pipe 
laying stays at 50%; the rework after the rain is halved. ${{protection.drainage_pump.priceUsd}} plus 
${{protection.drainage_pump.dailyUsd}} a day [to validate] | Count the open-trench tokens (Rules); is the sky to the 
south dark (Site); forecast percentage in the inbox (Plan) |
Paper\manual_v0.md:288:**Permits.** A zone opens to excavation when Plan enters the zone's permit code and the zone 
board posts the permit number. The city allows {{city.openTrenchLimitZones}} zone(s) open at a time. Excavation that 
reaches an unpermitted boundary waits there and bills; excavation that crosses one is pushing ahead (deviation F2) and 
draws a city fine of ${{rules.permitFineUsd}} [to validate].
Paper\manual_v0.md:308:**Machines (LOB-Game catalog).** Idle machines bill. Mobilization $25,000 per order; a released 
machine refunds half its price.
